On Thursday, June 20, 2013 5:56:57 PM UTC+4, clifford wrote:
>
> I am assuming that person for Lojban is defined around {cusku}.  People 
> not involved in the current utterance, either as intended source or 
> intended audience, are third person, by definition, again.  A person 
> doesn't have to be present to fill a first or second person role, doesn't 
> even have to be alive, apparently.
>

And "we" can include third persons not involved in the dialog. "We (that 
guy over there and I) will do it".
 

>
>
